21	 * so it does not depend on other owners or on creation order. The telephone has already been
22	 * normalized to E.164 form by {@link ValidateOwnerFields} before this step runs.
23	 *
24	 * <p>Should the deterministic code collide with an existing owner's {@code customerCode}, it is
25	 * de-duplicated by appending {@code -<n>} with the smallest {@code n} of 2 or more that makes it
26	 * unique (e.g. {@code NSW-1A2B3C4D}, then {@code NSW-1A2B3C4D-2}, {@code NSW-1A2B3C4D-3}, …).
27	 */
